cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this project and the upstream manuscript. This is a conditional
  research draft; include the repository commit used until a release is archived.
title: "A sharper exponent for integer multiplication"
authors:
  - family-names: Colkitt
    given-names: Douglas
  - family-names: Prosz
    given-names: Aurel
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Paureel/integer-mult-bounds"
url: "https://github.com/Paureel/integer-mult-bounds"
abstract: >-
  Conditional integer-multiplication refinement with an orthogonal-star complex
  network developed by Aurel Prosz, building on Douglas Colkitt's compact-control
  layer and OpenAI's pinned manuscript. The independently reconstructed finite
  implementation, exact certificates and combined source patch support
  kappa = 591/10^12 > 2^-31 under the retained algorithmic interfaces and supplied
  written proofs. The original conversation archive was unavailable during
  integration. The complete original multiplication theorem is assumed;
  independent expert review and formal verification are not supplied.
keywords:
  - integer multiplication
  - computational complexity
  - exact arithmetic
  - parameter optimization
  - reproducible research
references:
